The function getLampBrightness has two parameters: switchOn, a bool that says whether the switch is on or off, and brightnessSetting, an int for the brightness I want (0 to 100). Inside, an if/else checks switchOn. If it’s true, the function returns brightnessSetting, so the lamp uses the brightness I chose. If it’s false, the function returns 0 no matter what brightnessSetting is, so the lamp stays off. The function returns an int, and that value gets stored in lampBrightness in setup(). Turning the switch off doesn’t change or erase brightnessSetting. It just isn’t used for the output while the switch is off.
